inistros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 44 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.949,92 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No implica que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que haya malas prácticas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen por sector o tipo de servicio.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 52 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 17.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.1 to 4.2. December accounts for 4% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 44 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,949.92 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or genuine needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts [1] and [3] to confirm they align with the body's needs. Review awardee A's contracts to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Look for patterns in December contracts to understand if timing influenced the decisions.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["ZzD0Rxq1PVJJ8Trn0ZPzLw%3D%3D","QfgtKlI20PRxseVhcqrkhw%3D%3D","5H9VFTH71hCP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}